WEBVTT

00:03.962 --> 00:05.797
Episode 6
1 Plus 2 Equals... Threat!

00:06.506 --> 00:09.509
<i>During times like this,
Hibiki Sakurama would...</i>

00:11.845 --> 00:14.848
Hey, everyone! We should make sure
the civilians are safe first...

00:23.023 --> 00:28.361
Hibiki, you're too naive.
It'll be quicker to kill the monsters.

00:30.071 --> 00:33.992
<i>Huh... You guys are doing better
than I expected, Rangers.</i>

00:34.576 --> 00:39.289
<i>Fine, I get it.
I should defeat you guys next, right?</i>

00:40.123 --> 00:41.791
<i>And one day,</i>

00:41.875 --> 00:44.586
<i>I'll bite and tear into
those guys' throats!</i>

00:47.505 --> 00:49.090
I'll deal with this one!

00:52.635 --> 00:55.221
Time's up!

00:55.305 --> 00:58.391
With that, the training
for the final exam has ended.

00:58.475 --> 01:00.393
Tomorrow onwards,
we'll begin the real test.

01:00.894 --> 01:02.896
Return to your respective rooms
to rest for today.

01:02.979 --> 01:03.980
Tsk.

01:04.439 --> 01:06.608
Huh? W-Wait!

01:06.691 --> 01:08.943
I said I was gonna deal
with that one just now, didn't I?

01:09.527 --> 01:11.571
It's not nice to take
someone else's credit!

01:12.238 --> 01:14.699
Why would I need to do that

01:14.783 --> 01:17.160
when I'm leading in kills
and by a large margin?

01:22.540 --> 01:26.795
That bastard!
I swear I'll kick his ass first thing.

01:27.629 --> 01:32.550
Hey. Did you hear anything
about the exam from Sakurama,

01:32.634 --> 01:34.135
XX?

01:34.219 --> 01:36.763
Don't you dare speak of my name so easily.

01:36.846 --> 01:40.141
Die, scum. Die so hard
that even immortality can't save you.

01:42.268 --> 01:43.603
You understand, don't you?

01:43.686 --> 01:45.688
If we want to defeat the Rangers,

01:45.772 --> 01:49.067
the priority is
to pass this exam successfully.

01:50.068 --> 01:52.737
<i>Those guys are inconsistent
in terms of their strengths.</i>

01:53.238 --> 01:55.323
<i>The ones I need to keep a lookout for
are Ishikawa,</i>

01:55.406 --> 01:58.576
<i>Yukino, Akebayashi, and Urabe.</i>

01:58.660 --> 02:00.787
<i>The remaining are nothing much.</i>

02:01.663 --> 02:02.831
<i>As for him...</i>

02:03.331 --> 02:05.542
He's the last person I'll ever lose to.

02:06.626 --> 02:08.753
You're free to get along
with them, but don't forget.

02:08.837 --> 02:09.838
What?

02:09.921 --> 02:12.090
We're monsters.

02:12.173 --> 02:15.844
Better not let me see you
come to a pathetic end.

02:16.886 --> 02:18.763
There's no way I'd forget that.

02:18.847 --> 02:20.473
<i>All these hardships
they've made me experience</i>

02:20.557 --> 02:22.225
<i>for the past 10-plus years...</i>

02:22.308 --> 02:24.853
<i>All surface-dwellers are my enemies.</i>

02:24.936 --> 02:26.354
<i>No matter who I'm up against,</i>

02:26.437 --> 02:28.523
I'll take them down.

02:33.778 --> 02:35.446
Go! Go! Loser Ranger!

03:59.989 --> 04:02.492
I'll now explain
the rules for the final examination.

04:02.575 --> 04:04.827
First, we divided everyone
into five different types

04:04.911 --> 04:07.330
based on the training up till yesterday.

04:07.413 --> 04:10.166
It's the five groups
that you're all familiar with.

04:10.917 --> 04:14.671
The combat service support specialists,
Pink Squad.

04:14.754 --> 04:18.591
Stealth specialists who attack enemies
from the shadows, Green Squad.

04:18.675 --> 04:22.845
The foundation and brains of the Rangers,
Yellow Squad.

04:22.929 --> 04:25.390
Management specialists
who look at the big picture

04:25.473 --> 04:27.684
and skilled in working with our peers,
Blue Squad.

04:28.184 --> 04:30.436
Monster extermination specialists

04:30.520 --> 04:33.356
who are solely focused on offense,
Red Squad.

04:33.439 --> 04:35.441
<i>I see how it is.</i>

04:35.525 --> 04:37.694
<i>In short, I just need
to fight him one-on-one and win.</i>

04:37.777 --> 04:40.113
You guys will have to stay
in this special field

04:40.196 --> 04:42.532
and defeat five monsters.

04:42.615 --> 04:44.284
M-Monsters?

04:44.367 --> 04:46.869
The monster actors will be played
by our Rangers on active duty.

04:48.162 --> 04:52.166
They each have one of the five keys
of different colors in their possession.

04:52.250 --> 04:55.169
Those who manage
to take a key and escape from the field

04:55.253 --> 04:57.839
will obtain the right to be scouted
by the respective squadrons.

04:57.922 --> 04:59.007
In short...

04:59.090 --> 05:03.094
if you cadets want to pass,
teamwork is necessary.

05:03.177 --> 05:04.679
Teamwork...

05:05.805 --> 05:07.181
You have three days.

05:07.265 --> 05:09.267
Think of it as an actual Sunday Showdown,

05:09.350 --> 05:12.145
and you are restricted
to 30 minutes each day.

05:12.228 --> 05:15.231
When the time is up, the bells installed
across various locations will ring

05:15.315 --> 05:17.400
to signal the end of the battle.

05:17.483 --> 05:19.652
From here onwards,
you'll be fighting in teams.

05:19.736 --> 05:22.905
I repeat, teamwork is necessary.

05:23.489 --> 05:25.825
Otherwise, there's absolutely no way
you'll be able to win

05:25.908 --> 05:28.077
against those people.

05:28.911 --> 05:30.747
Now then, you may begin!

05:35.335 --> 05:37.754
For now, let's hide.
- We'll search for the monster actor.

05:37.837 --> 05:38.838
For god's sake...

05:38.921 --> 05:41.758
We have three days,
so let's go into hiding first.

05:41.841 --> 05:44.635
What kind of Ranger
sneaks around monsters?

05:44.719 --> 05:46.179
We'll fight them head-on.

05:46.262 --> 05:48.014
Wha...

05:50.350 --> 05:53.186
<i>I wouldn't have any trouble
if I could do that!</i>

05:53.269 --> 05:56.397
<i>I'm a goner
the moment I get hit a single time.</i>

05:57.190 --> 06:00.902
I joined the Rangers
to exterminate monsters,

06:00.985 --> 06:04.072
unlike you who's all about
talking things out with them.

06:04.155 --> 06:06.491
<i>This guy's a real pain in the ass,</i>

06:06.574 --> 06:08.576
<i>and in a different way from Sakurama.</i>

06:08.659 --> 06:10.828
<i>And I have to be with him for three days?</i>

06:11.537 --> 06:12.705
I understand.

06:13.247 --> 06:15.833
Let's search
for Red Squad's monster actor.

06:15.917 --> 06:17.710
Then call me over once you find them.

06:17.794 --> 06:21.672
Hold on. We have to move around in twos.

06:21.756 --> 06:24.467
- Tsk.
- The instructor said it, didn't he?

06:24.550 --> 06:26.594
Teamwork is necessary.

06:26.677 --> 06:28.930
If you aren't confident
in your own skills, then get lost!

06:29.013 --> 06:30.139
Come again?

06:30.223 --> 06:32.475
I don't care about this exam.

06:32.558 --> 06:35.770
I have my sights set on what's beyond it.

06:35.853 --> 06:37.772
Oh, you're one of those guys, aren't you?

06:37.855 --> 06:40.358
You want people to fawn over you
during Sunday Showdowns.

06:40.441 --> 06:42.276
Huh?

06:42.402 --> 06:43.403
Found you.

06:43.486 --> 06:44.904
Huh?

06:44.987 --> 06:47.657
<i>Y-Yumeko Suzukiri!</i>

06:48.908 --> 06:51.327
Oh? This isn't Yellow Squad.

06:51.411 --> 06:52.954
But I'm sorry.

06:53.037 --> 06:57.125
<i>I'm a fearsome monster
that attacks anyone I see.</i>

06:58.126 --> 07:00.169
<i>You better punish me, okay?</i>

07:00.253 --> 07:01.921
The monster actors...

07:02.004 --> 07:03.464
Are Junior First Rank Rangers?

07:03.548 --> 07:06.926
Wait. Suzukiri, do you have
the key for Yellow Squad?

07:07.009 --> 07:08.594
But we're in the Red Squad,

07:08.678 --> 07:10.012
so we don't plan on fighting you...

07:10.096 --> 07:11.097
Hey!

07:11.180 --> 07:13.766
Naive. How naive!
- Eh?

07:13.850 --> 07:16.936
You sure you can afford to say
something so half-assed?

07:17.019 --> 07:19.313
Ta-dah! The monster makes his appearance!

07:19.397 --> 07:21.190
Prepare yourselves,

07:21.274 --> 07:23.276
the abominable Rangers!

07:23.359 --> 07:24.527
<i>Tokita?</i>

07:27.029 --> 07:28.197
<i>Bingo!</i>

07:28.281 --> 07:30.366
<i>This guy's the monster actor
for Red Squad?</i>

07:30.450 --> 07:33.453
Hey, Replacement!
You seem really into this.

07:34.203 --> 07:37.290
But a two-on-two
is probably disadvantageous for you guys.

07:37.373 --> 07:38.541
What should I do?

07:38.624 --> 07:41.627
Huh? Wait, Shion...

07:45.006 --> 07:46.591
Owie...

07:47.175 --> 07:51.053
Yukino. She's not dead, is she?

07:52.555 --> 07:54.640
Aw, what a shame.

07:54.724 --> 07:58.019
I wanted to play with Sakurama
a little longer.

07:58.102 --> 07:59.145
I hear...

07:59.228 --> 08:00.229
Something too.

08:02.773 --> 08:07.320
<i>Damn, I'm late.
To think I'd meet him again...</i>

08:07.403 --> 08:09.447
<i>It doesn't matter who I'm up against.</i>

08:09.530 --> 08:13.618
<i>I've beaten him before,
and it's two against one this time.</i>

08:16.078 --> 08:17.330
Where's the key?

08:17.413 --> 08:19.165
I'm a monster, so I'm not telling...

08:19.248 --> 08:21.542
...you!

08:22.251 --> 08:23.461
Not too shabby.

08:23.586 --> 08:26.255
I've heard things about you.

08:26.839 --> 08:27.924
Something about a ranker

08:28.007 --> 08:30.510
who got all beat up
and lost to a mere Fighter.

08:31.177 --> 08:34.764
Red Senior Third Rank, Shun Tokita.
That's you, isn't it?

08:34.847 --> 08:37.183
The disgrace of the Rangers!

08:48.611 --> 08:50.238
Come on now!

08:51.572 --> 08:54.242
You don't need to worry about me.

08:54.325 --> 08:56.494
As you can see, I'm injured.

08:56.577 --> 09:01.082
But dealing with you guys
is almost like child's play to me.

09:01.165 --> 09:04.919
<i>At this rate,
you guys ain't ever gonna win.</i>

09:05.002 --> 09:08.923
Are you next, Hibiki?

09:14.637 --> 09:16.889
Hibiki.

09:16.973 --> 09:20.434
Are you just gonna stand there
and stare at the monster?

09:20.518 --> 09:22.103
This takes me back.

09:22.186 --> 09:25.439
The last time we played together
was back at the orphanage.

09:25.523 --> 09:28.693
Let's see how the little kid
who's all talk about becoming a hero

09:28.776 --> 09:30.945
has grown.

09:31.028 --> 09:33.364
<i>I can't count on that guy anymore.</i>

09:33.447 --> 09:35.950
<i>I'll have to do this myself. But...</i>

09:36.617 --> 09:39.662
<i>the moment I get hit,
my cover's gonna be blown immediately.</i>

09:40.413 --> 09:42.415
I'll give this one thing to you.

09:42.498 --> 09:43.874
It's a common weapon

09:43.958 --> 09:46.085
made by the Yellow Squadron
that all Rangers have.

09:46.168 --> 09:47.587
It's the Dragon Gadget!

09:47.670 --> 09:52.091
I only have nothing but bad memories
with this stupid thing!

09:52.174 --> 09:54.093
Please don't break it right away!

09:54.176 --> 09:55.970
I think if I do this...

09:56.804 --> 10:00.099
Dragon Gadget, Gun Form!

10:03.352 --> 10:04.353
You suck at this!

10:04.437 --> 10:06.105
Whoa!

10:15.740 --> 10:17.408
You're still around?

10:17.491 --> 10:20.661
I thought you'd already run away
with your tail between your legs.

10:20.745 --> 10:23.080
I’m not letting it end with my defeat!

10:23.164 --> 10:25.291
<i>What now?</i>

10:25.374 --> 10:26.375
Fire extinguisher

10:30.963 --> 10:31.964
Hit it!

10:33.674 --> 10:35.134
You missed, dumbass.

10:40.931 --> 10:42.767
Let’s withdraw for now and reorganize.

10:42.850 --> 10:44.477
Don't get in my way.

10:44.560 --> 10:47.647
You're all beaten up like this
because you charged in all alone!

10:48.230 --> 10:53.319
I won't work with anyone.
Especially not with a weakling like you.

10:53.402 --> 10:54.403
What?

10:55.071 --> 10:58.532
I'll win an official Ranger position,
no matter what it takes.

10:58.616 --> 11:00.576
Otherwise...

11:01.661 --> 11:04.330
...I won't be able to kill that monster.

11:04.413 --> 11:06.707
"That monster"?

11:09.168 --> 11:13.506
Give me a break already.
That ain't poisonous or anything, right?

11:13.589 --> 11:14.590
Damn you!

11:14.674 --> 11:16.884
I told you! You can't win one-on-one!

11:16.967 --> 11:18.511
Stop bothering me!

11:22.598 --> 11:24.183
<i>Don't push, don't push.
You better not push me!</i>

11:24.266 --> 11:26.352
<i>Yeah, I won't, I won't.
No, you should be pushing me!</i>

11:31.732 --> 11:32.733
Tsk.

11:32.817 --> 11:36.320
Wow, someone's having
a real flashy fight over there.

11:36.821 --> 11:38.823
I should end things here now.

11:38.906 --> 11:40.324
This lukewarm game of playing house

11:40.408 --> 11:42.451
isn't even good enough
for my physical rehabilitation!

11:42.535 --> 11:43.536
Shion!

11:43.619 --> 11:44.704
Shut up!

11:44.787 --> 11:47.707
If you're gonna run away with your tail
between your legs, do it alone!

11:47.790 --> 11:49.500
I understand.
- Huh?

11:49.583 --> 11:53.421
Just do whatever you want!
I don't care what happens to you!

11:53.504 --> 11:56.924
- Tsk.
- Hey, you guys shouldn't quarrel!

11:57.007 --> 12:01.178
Leave it! He's already given up
on winning from the start.

12:02.513 --> 12:05.599
I don't need him, I'll be fine on my own!

12:05.683 --> 12:07.685
Hah! How promising.

12:07.768 --> 12:09.520
But that's far from enough

12:09.603 --> 12:11.439
to pass the exam!

12:23.033 --> 12:26.829
Hey, hey! Where did
all your bravado from earlier go, huh?

12:26.912 --> 12:30.082
Who said that he can do this alone?

12:33.419 --> 12:35.588
Whoa, that was close.

12:42.178 --> 12:43.846
Oh, scary.

12:43.929 --> 12:45.306
Too bad.

12:45.389 --> 12:48.642
If only you'd passed, you'd be
the perfect candidate for Red Squadron.

12:48.726 --> 12:51.145
Well, you can try again next year...

12:51.228 --> 12:52.354
Huh?

13:08.287 --> 13:10.831
Hisui? What the hell
are you doing interrupting us?

13:10.915 --> 13:16.378
What? Your guy got in my way,
so I was doing the cleanup.

13:19.757 --> 13:22.259
Did you want a serious fight?

13:22.343 --> 13:23.344
What?

13:23.427 --> 13:26.013
If you're gonna play the monster,
then you should stick to the role.

13:26.096 --> 13:27.932
Those guys won't say things like that.

13:29.350 --> 13:32.269
No matter what you do,
it's fine as long as you win.

13:32.353 --> 13:37.650
Everything the winner does is forgiven,
while the losers are as good as dust.

13:38.234 --> 13:41.237
Man, this is a pain.

13:41.320 --> 13:45.366
I was hoping to deal
with those two quickly and go back.

13:47.493 --> 13:50.996
I can't believe there's double the trash
to deal with now.

13:51.121 --> 13:55.459
What will you do?
There are two monster actors now.

13:56.043 --> 14:00.214
We're 100 times more vicious
than the real deal!

14:02.925 --> 14:04.426
All right, time for a scuffle!

14:04.510 --> 14:08.097
Let's spread out in all four directions
and surround them both!

14:08.180 --> 14:09.223
Got it!

14:15.563 --> 14:17.231
<i>This one's done for.</i>

14:17.314 --> 14:19.275
- I won't let it end.
- What?

14:19.358 --> 14:24.655
I don't want to let things end
before I even get to fulfill my duty...

14:26.240 --> 14:28.492
Shion! Do you know how to draw?

14:29.076 --> 14:30.077
What?

14:30.160 --> 14:31.453
What about you, Ishikawa?

14:31.537 --> 14:34.331
No, not at all...

14:34.915 --> 14:36.041
What about you, Usukubo?

14:38.002 --> 14:39.086
Oh...

14:43.257 --> 14:46.552
What a drag. You've got it good.

14:46.635 --> 14:47.970
You're not a Junior First Rank,

14:48.053 --> 14:50.222
so you don't have to do this again
next year.

14:50.306 --> 14:53.851
What? I'll be a Senior First Rank by then.

14:55.019 --> 14:57.855
The chance of that happening is even lower
than them passing this exam.

15:03.777 --> 15:05.654
Tsk. How boring.

15:05.738 --> 15:08.991
How long are they planning
to keep up with this game?

15:16.624 --> 15:18.000
What?

15:18.626 --> 15:19.835
Huh?

15:20.419 --> 15:23.714
It's you, Tokita. Where did those guys go?

15:23.797 --> 15:26.342
Wha... Hey!

15:32.556 --> 15:34.475
Found you!

15:36.560 --> 15:39.396
Oh! Sorry, I messed up.

15:39.480 --> 15:41.523
Do that again and I'll kill you.

15:41.607 --> 15:43.359
Sorry about that.

15:47.738 --> 15:50.282
Well, I'm not really confident
in my drawing skills.

15:50.366 --> 15:54.620
Really? Still, considering
that we're in the midst of all the smoke...

15:54.703 --> 15:56.538
Thanks, I'll take them.

15:56.622 --> 15:59.625
Oh, wait! I think they're really bad!

15:59.708 --> 16:03.045
I drew them in a rush, so the drawings
are all messed up and rough!

16:03.128 --> 16:04.630
Usukubo,

16:04.713 --> 16:08.217
I think you're better off quitting Rangers
and becoming an artist instead.

16:08.300 --> 16:10.636
Now that gives me mixed feelings.

16:10.719 --> 16:12.888
But are those helpful?

16:12.972 --> 16:14.723
Yeah. They really are.

16:15.474 --> 16:18.894
Sakurama. What are you planning
to do with those?

16:19.603 --> 16:21.355
I'll let them know something.

16:22.189 --> 16:25.943
<i>Time to let the imposters know
how scary the real deal is.</i>

16:27.319 --> 16:33.075
<i>Those guys... They aren't scary.
They're just strong.</i>

16:40.874 --> 16:41.875
Oh.

16:41.959 --> 16:45.129
Tsk. Again? This is getting irritating.

16:45.212 --> 16:46.338
Hey!

16:46.422 --> 16:49.091
Don't just stand there blankly.

16:49.174 --> 16:50.634
You know they’re just hoping

16:50.718 --> 16:52.845
that we’d end up taking
each other down, right?

16:52.928 --> 16:54.346
You stupid-- Whoa!

16:54.430 --> 16:57.558
Hey! You little twerp...

16:57.641 --> 16:59.810
Enough.

16:59.893 --> 17:02.104
Why do you keep doing this?

17:02.187 --> 17:04.273
I warned you that there's no next time,
didn't I?

17:04.356 --> 17:08.277
Huh? The hell are you talking about?
Get your act together, Hisui--

17:10.070 --> 17:14.241
This is annoying.
I'll deal with you first.

17:14.324 --> 17:18.704
Also, I may be a spunky high school girl
who's younger than you,

17:18.787 --> 17:20.873
but I'm three ranks higher!

17:20.956 --> 17:22.750
Use your honorifics, damn it!

17:22.833 --> 17:25.210
<i>Is she for real?</i>

17:27.588 --> 17:29.923
I'm charging in. Please follow me.

17:30.007 --> 17:31.925
What? Who'd follow you...

17:32.009 --> 17:35.929
Is that so?
In that case, feel free to rest.

17:36.013 --> 17:38.515
If possible, do it somewhere
that won't get in my way.

17:38.599 --> 17:42.519
Th-The hell did you say? Ow...

17:43.270 --> 17:45.898
You're injured, so it's not like
I can count on you or anything.

17:45.981 --> 17:49.151
It'll only be trouble if you hold me back.

17:49.234 --> 17:52.071
You said
you won't work with anyone, right?

17:52.154 --> 17:55.157
I'll send those words right back at you.

17:55.240 --> 17:57.451
Especially not with weaklings.

17:57.534 --> 18:01.163
You little...

18:04.249 --> 18:08.087
Man, that hurt...

18:09.838 --> 18:12.466
Oh, no! Are you all right?

18:12.549 --> 18:15.177
You bastard...

18:15.260 --> 18:18.305
You keep getting hit on the left side.

18:18.388 --> 18:21.475
Don't tell me it's hard to see?

18:23.477 --> 18:27.189
Take this! Invisible Shot!

18:32.027 --> 18:34.696
Whoa, that was close!

18:34.780 --> 18:36.949
Come on! What's wrong?

18:37.032 --> 18:39.034
Is that all?

18:40.035 --> 18:45.707
If you're gonna call for help,
now's your chance, little kid.

18:45.791 --> 18:47.960
Unfortunately, that choice
is completely off the table

18:48.043 --> 18:49.962
because of a certain someone.

18:50.045 --> 18:52.840
Shion, you mustn't come!

18:52.923 --> 18:55.217
You can't take him on as you are now.

18:55.300 --> 18:58.971
I'll be fine,
so please get back!

19:00.180 --> 19:03.183
You're still saying naive stuff like that?

19:06.687 --> 19:08.355
Well, that's fine.

19:08.438 --> 19:12.359
As you wish,
you'll be withdrawing from the fight here!

19:13.944 --> 19:17.364
I told you to get back, didn't I?

19:17.447 --> 19:19.032
<i>Don't push, don't push.
You better not push me!</i>

19:19.116 --> 19:22.119
<i>Yeah, I won't, I won't.
No, you should be pushing me!</i>

19:22.202 --> 19:24.204
If I said not to push, you'll push.

19:24.288 --> 19:26.623
And if I tell you to get back,
you won't get back. Right?

19:33.338 --> 19:34.381
Bam!

19:40.596 --> 19:43.765
You're surprisingly really simple to read.

19:43.849 --> 19:46.310
I'm just here to get back at him.

19:46.977 --> 19:49.938
But it's just one punch after all that,
so it's not really worth it.

19:50.772 --> 19:52.441
Should I go easy on you?

19:52.524 --> 19:53.984
I'll kill you!

19:54.067 --> 19:55.944
This is making me cry.

19:56.028 --> 19:57.112
Unlike the Red Squadron,

19:57.196 --> 20:01.200
the Green Squadron's an obscure team
that doesn't stand out.

20:02.034 --> 20:05.204
Still, it's sad for us to be forgotten.

20:05.287 --> 20:06.580
Hisui!

20:06.663 --> 20:10.000
You forgot the "san"!

20:16.924 --> 20:19.927
She's handling the two of them so easily...

20:20.010 --> 20:21.845
Sorry to keep you waiting.

20:22.471 --> 20:23.889
You're next.

20:24.473 --> 20:26.850
I didn't expect you to come this far,
to be honest.

20:26.934 --> 20:31.396
This has gotten a little more exciting
thanks to you, Sakurama's little brother.

20:36.568 --> 20:38.946
<i>Is she for real?</i>

20:43.867 --> 20:45.535
Soujirou!

20:49.456 --> 20:53.210
I won't give up!
Not until I join your squadron!

21:00.050 --> 21:04.805
Huh. You have a better look
on your face now.

21:06.848 --> 21:11.395
Thanks! Because of you guys,
I get to win this guy again!

21:11.478 --> 21:13.897
You little shit!

21:13.981 --> 21:15.315
You...

21:15.399 --> 21:18.068
This is child's play, right?
Then play along with us.

22:50.952 --> 22:52.954
Translated by Qianni Lu

22:55.874 --> 22:57.000
You...

23:04.716 --> 23:08.011
Hah! Headshots don't count, dumbass!

23:08.095 --> 23:11.681
Fine by me!

23:26.530 --> 23:30.325
<i>Time's up!
The first day of the final exam ends here!</i>

23:32.494 --> 23:36.706
The road here is kinda in a zig-zag.
I want to walk in a straight path!

23:36.790 --> 23:38.375
You'll fail if you do that.
What?

23:38.458 --> 23:40.419
<i>Next episode,
"The Zigzag Road to the Final Exam!"</i>

23:40.502 --> 23:42.921
- I'll fail...
- Come on! Do this properly! Properly!

23:43.004 --> 23:44.005
O-Ouch! Thank you!

23:44.089 --> 23:46.925
- The game ends when you give up!
- I'll fail...
